      "problem": "A lunch combo costs $$27$ before tax. If a $7%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total price after tax?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the total price after tax, we apply a $7%$ increase to the original cost.\n\nIncreasing by $7%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+7%=107%=1.07\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.07:$\n\n$$\n27\\times 1.07=28.89.\n$$\n\nSo, the total price after tax is $$28.89.$",
